/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts


# .claude — ONLY the three agents the CI reviewers invoke are tracked (D1,
# context/features/ci-cd-pr-pipeline.md). Everything else stays local: agent-memory/ is
# unattended-run output no human has read, settings.local.json is machine-specific, skills/
# read context/ files that are not in the repo, and coder/code-scanner are invoked by no
# workflow. The never-stage-.claude habit is now a rule: `git add .claude` cannot sweep them in.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/pr-reviewer.md
!.claude/agents/auth-auditor.md
!.claude/agents/ui-reviewer.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
!context/*
!context/project-overview.md
!context/current-feature.md
INSTRUCTIONS.md
logs
audit-results


subdomain-routing-setup.md

.playwright-mcp
skills-lock.json
.mcp.json


/src/generated/prisma
